# =====================================================================
# LINE ENDINGS
# =====================================================================
# Windows ends a line with CR+LF, Linux with LF alone. Git stores bytes,
# so the same text saved on two machines is two different files as far as
# a diff is concerned - every line reads as changed.
#
# Without this file that is decided by each contributor's local
# core.autocrlf setting, which is why this repository ended up storing
# four files as CRLF and eleven as LF, and why a six-line fix to db.py
# rendered on GitHub as "2 insertions, 176 deletions".
#
# .gitattributes is committed, so it applies to everyone who clones -
# unlike core.autocrlf, which only ever applied to one machine.
#
# Everything is normalised to LF in the repository. The daemon runs on
# Linux, Python does not care either way, and every current editor on
# Windows handles LF correctly.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

* text=auto eol=lf

# Source and documentation: always LF, never converted.
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf

# Windows batch files. cmd.exe is happier with CRLF, and these are only
# ever run on Windows, so they are the one exception to the LF rule above.
*.bat   text eol=crlf

# Binary: never touch the bytes. Newline conversion inside an archive or
# an audio file would corrupt it silently and permanently.
*.zip   binary
*.rar   binary
*.flac  binary
*.mp3   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.ico   binary

# =====================================================================
# WHAT DOES NOT LEAVE THIS REPOSITORY
# =====================================================================
# `git archive` is how the public tree is extracted, and export-ignore is
# the only thing that makes "internal only" mean anything to it. Without a
# rule here, a file is internal by intention and public in fact.
#
# docs/UPDATES.md is the full internal changelog: 50KB, written against
# this repository's own PR and issue numbers and branch names, none of
# which resolve anywhere outside it. docs/UPDATES-PUBLIC.md is the version
# that ships. Before this rule the internal one was in the archive, and it
# still named a real channel.
docs/UPDATES.md    export-ignore
